<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cetina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cetina is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, flowing about 100 kilometres from the Dinaric mountains to the Adriatic at Omiš. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it marked the western limit of the Narentine principality of Pagania, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poljica">Poljica</a> district lay between its lower course and the coast; it later formed a frontier of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cetina.jpg" alt="Cetina" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nikolaj Potanin · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cetina_river.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
